1
00:00:25,940 --> 00:00:29,880
YAMU! YAMU! YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,660
Your moves!

3
00:01:31,380 --> 00:01:32,210
Yeah!

4
00:01:32,293 --> 00:01:33,702
All that dueling made me hungry.

5
00:01:33,860 --> 00:01:36,677
Did any of you guys remember
to bring any food with you?

6
00:01:36,760 --> 00:01:37,590
Sorry, Joe.

7
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:42,457
What were we thinking
coming here with no food?

8
00:01:42,540 --> 00:01:44,037
How were we ever going
to get through the rest

9
00:01:44,120 --> 00:01:46,017
of the competition
without anything to eat?

10
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:47,777
That's a good question, Joey.

11
00:01:47,860 --> 00:01:49,677
This dueling really takes it out of you,

12
00:01:49,760 --> 00:01:53,617
and I haven't seen any burger stands
or restaurants since we got here.

13
00:01:53,700 --> 00:01:55,317
Well, we better do something fast.

14
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:59,812
I've got to have my five basic food
groups or else it's metabolic meltdown!

15
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:01,457
Hey, chill out, you guys.

16
00:02:01,540 --> 00:02:04,300
I got it covered. Yeah? Check it out.

17
00:02:04,440 --> 00:02:06,381
The Great Outdoor Survival Guide.

18
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:07,540
Can we eat it?

19
00:02:07,680 --> 00:02:08,680
Better than that.

20
00:02:08,780 --> 00:02:12,017
It lists all the plants, roots,
berries, and grasses we can eat.

21
00:02:12,100 --> 00:02:12,930
Ew!

22
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:16,040
Do I look like a squirrel, you big doofus?

23
00:02:17,100 --> 00:02:19,300
I don't need your dumb book anyhow.

24
00:02:19,700 --> 00:02:21,876
I smell something cooking that-a-way.

25
00:02:22,700 --> 00:02:23,530
See ya.

26
00:02:25,220 --> 00:02:26,338
He's hallucinating.

27
00:02:26,540 --> 00:02:27,517
Don't be so sure.

28
00:02:27,600 --> 00:02:31,188
You know, it wasn't his brain
that beat Mai, it was his nose.

29
00:02:35,640 --> 00:02:38,700
Oh, man, I just love
barbecued fish. Smells good.

30
00:02:38,900 --> 00:02:41,135
Yeah, and I bet it tastes even better.

31
00:02:41,740 --> 00:02:44,237
What makes you think those
fish are yours to eat?

32
00:02:44,320 --> 00:02:47,400
Hey, trust me, we eat first
and ask questions later.

33
00:02:47,580 --> 00:02:49,168
His stomachs will thank me.

34
00:02:51,060 --> 00:02:51,890
Joey?

35
00:02:51,973 --> 00:02:53,957
Oh, he'd say anything to fill his belly.

36
00:02:54,040 --> 00:02:57,360
Some people have absolutely
no self-control. Huh?

37
00:02:57,760 --> 00:02:59,540
Joey, save some for me.

38
00:03:04,160 --> 00:03:05,807
Ah, man, this looks awesome.

39
00:03:06,040 --> 00:03:07,275
Ow, ow, ow, hot, hot.

40
00:03:10,220 --> 00:03:12,440
Ready, set, feeding frenzy.

41
00:03:13,780 --> 00:03:15,637
Enjoy yourselves, you fish thieves.

42
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:17,073
This is your last meal.

43
00:03:20,160 --> 00:03:23,440
How dare you eat my fish,
you thieving poachers.

44
00:03:23,620 --> 00:03:25,385
Has no one taught you manners?

45
00:03:29,140 --> 00:03:34,397
so can we eat now all right let's try that

46
00:03:34,480 --> 00:03:37,420
one more time i knew this was a bad idea

47
00:03:38,360 --> 00:03:42,997
how dare you steal my fish you
bottom feeding thieves hey chill out

48
00:03:43,080 --> 00:03:47,157
guy it's just a few fish a few fish
that do not belong to you and to

49
00:03:47,240 --> 00:03:50,877
steal a fisherman's catch is to
prove you have no honor a dueling

50
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:56,600
glove wait a second aren't you mako
tsunami the top rank ocean duelist

51
00:03:57,480 --> 00:03:59,060
And who might you be?

52
00:03:59,440 --> 00:04:01,297
Yeah, you're that freaky fish guy.

53
00:04:01,380 --> 00:04:03,400
I am not a freaky fish guy.

54
00:04:04,220 --> 00:04:08,060
I am Mako Tsunami, duelist
extraordinaire of the seven seas.

55
00:04:10,200 --> 00:04:12,260
Uh, what are you laughing about?

56
00:04:12,640 --> 00:04:13,740
Your head.

57
00:04:14,280 --> 00:04:15,660
You've got company.

58
00:04:16,220 --> 00:04:17,050
Huh?

59
00:04:19,420 --> 00:04:20,700
Off with you!

60
00:04:21,780 --> 00:04:23,080
No, don't!

61
00:04:23,220 --> 00:04:24,397
I wanted to eat that.

62
00:04:24,480 --> 00:04:25,421
You're demented.

63
00:04:25,960 --> 00:04:29,480
Are you telling me that those
two are here as duelists?

64
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,100
I'm Yugi Moto.

65
00:04:31,400 --> 00:04:32,694
Sorry about your fish.

66
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:33,950
You?

67
00:04:34,033 --> 00:04:38,580
You're Yugi Moto, the only duelist
to ever defeat Seto Kaiba? Ha ha!

68
00:04:38,820 --> 00:04:39,917
What a fine surprise!

69
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:43,160
It will be my very great
honor to face you in a duel!

70
00:04:43,860 --> 00:04:45,220
Same here, Mako.

71
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:46,460
I must apologize.

72
00:04:46,560 --> 00:04:47,795
I've been ungracious.

73
00:04:48,060 --> 00:04:51,117
If you are friends of Yugi
Moto, please come sit down.

74
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:52,030
Eat your fill.

75
00:04:52,113 --> 00:04:52,943
Thanks!

76
00:04:53,026 --> 00:04:53,856
You are welcome.

77
00:04:54,140 --> 00:04:54,970
Hey!

78
00:04:55,053 --> 00:04:55,883
Feeding, Frenzy!

79
00:04:58,420 --> 00:05:01,600
Oh, man, Freaky Fish Guy
really knows how to cook.

80
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:04,440
It's really good, huh? Mm-hmm.

81
00:05:07,460 --> 00:05:08,820
Wow, that was good.

82
00:05:08,960 --> 00:05:11,078
Where'd you learn to cook like that?

83
00:05:11,740 --> 00:05:14,800
I have had to fend for
myself since I was a tadpole,

84
00:05:14,980 --> 00:05:17,997
but it was my father who
taught me how to fish and cook.

85
00:05:18,080 --> 00:05:20,757
So, what brings you
here to the competition?

86
00:05:20,840 --> 00:05:25,740
I was raised on a fishing boat where I
learned to love the sea, so if I win here,

87
00:05:25,940 --> 00:05:28,000
I would love a vessel of my own.

88
00:05:28,260 --> 00:05:31,201
Of course, I'll have to
beat a few duelists first.

89
00:05:32,220 --> 00:05:33,300
Your own boat?

90
00:05:33,420 --> 00:05:37,008
How great would that be, living
life out on the big blue sea?

91
00:05:37,180 --> 00:05:41,677
Yes, the ocean is amazing, and we have
shared a special bond since I was born.

92
00:05:41,760 --> 00:05:44,937
I can tell when the sea is
happy by the way it sparkles,

93
00:05:45,020 --> 00:05:49,160
and when it is angry
by the shifting tides.

94
00:05:50,360 --> 00:05:53,700
Excuse me, I did not mean
to be so serious Oh, no,

95
00:05:53,920 --> 00:05:55,837
don't apologize You saved our hides,

96
00:05:55,920 --> 00:05:58,817
we'd be starving without you
This has really been great

97
00:05:58,900 --> 00:05:59,780
Thanks again

98
00:06:00,660 --> 00:06:02,640
Leaving so soon, are you?

99
00:06:02,760 --> 00:06:06,348
Nice meeting you, Mako Maybe
we'll meet up in the competition

100
00:06:08,060 --> 00:06:09,500
We certainly will

101
00:06:10,920 --> 00:06:12,802
Sooner than you think, my friend

102
00:06:18,280 --> 00:06:23,397
I treated you to dinner
perhaps you will honor me with

103
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:28,077
a duel he's nuts no but I am
an expert fisherman and you

104
00:06:28,160 --> 00:06:34,437
have taken my bait why the
fish of course I laid it out

105
00:06:34,520 --> 00:06:39,637
and lured you three right in
but i never expected to catch

106
00:06:39,720 --> 00:06:43,697
yugi moto ah forget this
crazy chicken in the sea yugi

107
00:06:43,780 --> 00:06:48,257
can't we just give the guy
back a few fish i reeled in

108
00:06:48,340 --> 00:06:51,297
another duelist a short time
ago but he was not a worthy

109
00:06:51,380 --> 00:06:55,800
opponent but a duel against
you yugi would be a true test

110
00:07:14,640 --> 00:07:17,760
Meiko Tsunami, I accept your challenge

111
00:07:20,100 --> 00:07:21,840
Behold, Yugi Moto

112
00:07:24,560 --> 00:07:27,800
We shall battle beside the majestic sea.

113
00:07:36,740 --> 00:07:39,980
The playing field is equally
split into two halves.

114
00:07:40,300 --> 00:07:42,560
One half is land, the other is sea.

115
00:07:43,580 --> 00:07:45,140
And the stakes, Mako?

116
00:07:45,340 --> 00:07:47,760
I wager two starships on this match.

117
00:07:48,160 --> 00:07:49,240
Two stars.

118
00:07:51,260 --> 00:07:56,557
finally an adversary of real merit
how i have waited for this day now

119
00:07:56,640 --> 00:08:01,457
let the battle begin this should

120
00:08:01,540 --> 00:08:04,437
be some match sink that soggy sucker

121
00:08:04,520 --> 00:08:10,057
yugi i'm curious to see how you
will combat my mighty denizens of

122
00:08:10,140 --> 00:08:14,737
the deep what's this his creature

123
00:08:14,820 --> 00:08:17,300
is underwater how do i choose which

124
00:08:17,820 --> 00:08:20,617
card to play when I can't
even see what I'm fighting.

125
00:08:20,700 --> 00:08:22,200
This I don't like.

126
00:08:22,640 --> 00:08:24,200
The ocean conceals

127
00:08:27,180 --> 00:08:29,537
many things beneath its shifting surface.

128
00:08:29,620 --> 00:08:33,340
As long as that thing stays
submerged, I can't attack.

129
00:08:33,680 --> 00:08:36,900
I promise he won't stay
submerged for very long.

130
00:08:37,140 --> 00:08:39,497
I have no idea what that
thing is down there,

131
00:08:39,580 --> 00:08:43,820
so I better prepare for the worst
with as strong a defense as possible.

132
00:08:44,520 --> 00:08:48,873
Hmm, clearly this is Yu-Gi's first
encounter with sea-based duel monsters.

133
00:08:48,960 --> 00:08:52,457
You will learn firsthand what
a powerful ally the sea can be.

134
00:08:52,540 --> 00:08:56,440
It gives my creatures a field
power bonus, and it conceals them,

135
00:08:56,640 --> 00:08:59,405
making their stealthy
attacks even more lethal.

136
00:08:59,640 --> 00:09:00,617
Something's fishy.

137
00:09:00,700 --> 00:09:02,457
How can he fight when he can't see?

138
00:09:02,540 --> 00:09:03,370
Beats me.

139
00:09:03,453 --> 00:09:05,080
This is totally bogus.

140
00:09:06,480 --> 00:09:10,857
It seems that my ocean-based strategy
has taken you by surprise, Yu-Gi.

141
00:09:10,940 --> 00:09:13,822
Maybe so, but I can still
raise a strong defense.

142
00:09:13,940 --> 00:09:16,660
I call upon the Horned Imp!

143
00:09:21,840 --> 00:09:24,660
Now, Fiend Kraken, ensnare him!

144
00:09:25,340 --> 00:09:26,170
My Imp!

145
00:09:32,680 --> 00:09:33,510
Attack!

146
00:09:34,360 --> 00:09:35,560
What is that?

147
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:38,480
Whatever it is, it's bad news for Yugi.

148
00:09:45,240 --> 00:09:46,260
Oh, man.

149
00:09:46,660 --> 00:09:48,013
Yugi's imp is done for.

150
00:09:48,700 --> 00:09:50,620
Fiend Kraken, end this now.

151
00:09:54,240 --> 00:09:56,100
Well done, Kraken.

152
00:09:58,240 --> 00:10:00,593
Wow, and that was just his opening move.

153
00:10:03,860 --> 00:10:05,017
You're good, Mako.

154
00:10:05,100 --> 00:10:06,517
A brilliant opening play.

155
00:10:06,600 --> 00:10:10,840
I am pleased you appreciate it,
though I very much doubt your imp did.

156
00:10:12,080 --> 00:10:14,256
Well, now I know what I'm up against.

157
00:10:14,340 --> 00:10:19,300
Yes, the mighty ocean commands respect,
as do the creatures that inhabit it.

158
00:10:19,560 --> 00:10:23,300
Maybe I can prepare an attack
that will destroy his creatures,

159
00:10:23,480 --> 00:10:25,200
even though I can't see them.

160
00:10:26,180 --> 00:10:27,180
Feral imp!

161
00:10:30,400 --> 00:10:33,677
My feral imp should dispense
with Mako's monsters,

162
00:10:33,760 --> 00:10:36,540
no matter how deep
they're hidden in the sea.

163
00:10:37,160 --> 00:10:41,380
I am familiar with your feral
monster, and it's electrical attack.

164
00:10:41,660 --> 00:10:46,700
So for my next card, I
play my giant jellyfish.

165
00:10:50,060 --> 00:10:50,890
Behold!

166
00:10:53,380 --> 00:10:55,360
I don't like the sound of that.

167
00:10:57,300 --> 00:10:59,535
That is the battle cry of my creature.

168
00:10:59,620 --> 00:11:00,877
It'll be crying, all right,

169
00:11:00,960 --> 00:11:04,900
once I combine my feral imp with
the magical horn of the unicorn.

170
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:15,700
All right. What?

171
00:11:16,400 --> 00:11:20,237
Yugi can't see Mako's monsters, but
he knows they're all underwater,

172
00:11:20,320 --> 00:11:22,137
and water conducts electricity.

173
00:11:22,220 --> 00:11:25,926
Oh, so they're vulnerable to the
feral imp's electrical attack.

174
00:11:26,020 --> 00:11:28,040
Whoa, that is so smart!

175
00:11:29,760 --> 00:11:31,640
Magic lightning, attack!

176
00:11:36,280 --> 00:11:37,680
It's a fish fry!

177
00:11:42,140 --> 00:11:45,460
But wait, what is this?
Nothing's happening.

178
00:11:45,620 --> 00:11:47,679
Mako still has all his life points.

179
00:11:48,520 --> 00:11:50,820
Your strategy has failed, Yugi.

180
00:11:51,620 --> 00:11:52,450
How?

181
00:11:52,980 --> 00:11:56,937
As a sea duelist, I am well aware
that water conducts electricity,

182
00:11:57,020 --> 00:11:59,560
so I played my giant jellyfish.

183
00:11:59,740 --> 00:12:03,197
It has the magical ability to
absorb all electrical attacks,

184
00:12:03,280 --> 00:12:05,620
protecting all of my ocean creatures.

185
00:12:07,880 --> 00:12:10,300
And now it's time for my counter-attack.

186
00:12:10,700 --> 00:12:13,240
Fiend Kraken, crush his feral limb!

187
00:12:19,360 --> 00:12:20,740
Crush him now!

188
00:12:25,300 --> 00:12:27,660
Did you enjoy my Kraken's embrace?

189
00:12:29,260 --> 00:12:31,917
I've never dueled against
creatures like these before.

190
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:34,777
It feels as if I'm battling
Mako's sea monsters

191
00:12:34,860 --> 00:12:37,680
and the awesome power of the ocean itself.

192
00:12:38,820 --> 00:12:43,360
Do any of your cards have the power
to stand against my ocean pets?

193
00:12:43,640 --> 00:12:46,000
I have the power of Silverfang,

194
00:12:46,240 --> 00:12:50,680
and I combine him with the magic of
the full moon to double his ferocity.

195
00:12:55,920 --> 00:12:56,960
Ferocious indeed.

196
00:12:57,060 --> 00:13:00,531
But the moon also controls the
tides, causing them to rise.

197
00:13:02,160 --> 00:13:04,720
Allowing me to unleash my next creature.

198
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:06,920
Arise, mighty Koryoshin!

199
00:13:09,980 --> 00:13:10,880
What's this?

200
00:13:15,600 --> 00:13:18,180
Whoa, that is one big fish!

201
00:13:18,660 --> 00:13:20,800
Behold the colossal Koryoshin,

202
00:13:20,920 --> 00:13:24,677
a creature so enormous that when
he rises up from the ocean depths,

203
00:13:24,760 --> 00:13:26,680
he creates his own tidal wave.

204
00:13:26,880 --> 00:13:27,820
What a beast!

205
00:13:28,560 --> 00:13:33,740
Your wolf is brave, Yugi, but he will not
stand before my Karyushin's title attack.

206
00:13:35,960 --> 00:13:37,560
No, Silver Fang!

207
00:13:40,540 --> 00:13:41,370
Gone.

208
00:13:41,540 --> 00:13:46,500
But my Karyushin's title attack did more
than simply wash your wolf cub away. What?

209
00:13:46,720 --> 00:13:49,720
It considerably altered our playing field.

210
00:13:49,920 --> 00:13:50,800
My land!

211
00:13:51,600 --> 00:13:56,180
Karyushin's attack has nearly washed
away my entire land-based playing field.

212
00:13:57,720 --> 00:14:00,180
You should consider yourself lucky, Yugi.

213
00:14:00,380 --> 00:14:02,937
In my previous duels,
when Kuryushin attacks,

214
00:14:03,020 --> 00:14:05,657
absolutely nothing is
left standing in its wake.

215
00:14:05,740 --> 00:14:08,157
I think it was quite
considerate of my pet to

216
00:14:08,240 --> 00:14:10,837
leave you a little patch
of dirt to stand on,

217
00:14:10,920 --> 00:14:11,750
don't you?

218
00:14:12,380 --> 00:14:16,380
Or does it make you uneasy to be
surrounded on all sides by the sea?

219
00:14:17,100 --> 00:14:21,180
All men give pause before the
savage power of the mighty ocean,

220
00:14:21,640 --> 00:14:23,464
even the greatest of fishermen.

221
00:14:23,680 --> 00:14:24,940
You mean your father?

222
00:14:25,460 --> 00:14:27,520
My father was a great fisherman.

223
00:14:28,060 --> 00:14:33,080
He taught me my love of the sea,
but one day the sea took him.

224
00:14:34,380 --> 00:14:37,017
I loved going out on
the boat with my father,

225
00:14:37,100 --> 00:14:39,960
just the two of us and
the big, beautiful ocean,

226
00:14:40,260 --> 00:14:43,080
never suspecting that
the sea would turn on us.

227
00:14:43,180 --> 00:14:46,800
Look, Mako, there's a storm
blowing in. A big one? Maybe.

228
00:14:47,080 --> 00:14:49,904
I've learned to never
take chances with the sea.

229
00:14:50,180 --> 00:14:51,010
Oh.

230
00:14:51,093 --> 00:14:51,923
And father was right.

231
00:14:52,160 --> 00:14:55,337
Suddenly, the calm, friendly sea
turned into a raging maelstrom.

232
00:14:55,420 --> 00:14:57,773
It pitched our boat as if it were a toy.

233
00:14:58,120 --> 00:14:59,680
Father, I can't hold on.

234
00:14:59,860 --> 00:15:00,900
It's okay, Mako.

235
00:15:02,320 --> 00:15:03,757
There, I've tied you down.

236
00:15:03,840 --> 00:15:04,877
You'll be safe here, son.

237
00:15:04,960 --> 00:15:05,790
I promise.

238
00:15:05,873 --> 00:15:06,703
Dad, look out.

239
00:15:12,020 --> 00:15:16,360
When the storm finally died out,
our little boat had washed ashore.

240
00:15:17,160 --> 00:15:18,500
My father was right.

241
00:15:18,760 --> 00:15:20,540
I had been perfectly safe.

242
00:15:20,820 --> 00:15:23,197
But because he had stopped to tie me down,

243
00:15:23,280 --> 00:15:26,060
He had no time to secure
himself to the mast.

244
00:15:26,880 --> 00:15:28,817
I thought I had lost him forever.

245
00:15:28,900 --> 00:15:31,537
But then I noticed that
our lifeboat was missing.

246
00:15:31,620 --> 00:15:33,500
I know my father is alive.

247
00:15:33,920 --> 00:15:39,340
So I will win this contest, buy a ship,
and search the seven seas until I find him.

248
00:15:39,760 --> 00:15:41,480
That is why I duel, Yugi.

249
00:15:41,660 --> 00:15:42,897
That is why I must win.

250
00:15:42,980 --> 00:15:44,340
And you must lose.

251
00:15:44,640 --> 00:15:46,640
I understand, Mako. Believe me.

252
00:15:46,740 --> 00:15:48,505
But I still can't let you win.

253
00:15:49,340 --> 00:15:50,170
Ha!

254
00:15:50,253 --> 00:15:51,083
Oh, wow.

255
00:15:51,166 --> 00:15:54,315
Mako duels for his dad like
Yugi duels for his grandpa.

256
00:15:54,640 --> 00:15:56,169
Whoa, this is too intense.

257
00:15:56,840 --> 00:16:00,717
With so little land left to me, I've
really got to make this next play count.

258
00:16:00,800 --> 00:16:03,682
I need something that will
help me turn the tide.

259
00:16:03,860 --> 00:16:05,331
Something like this card.

260
00:16:05,660 --> 00:16:07,420
Giant Soldier of Stone.

261
00:16:10,760 --> 00:16:13,878
You may have shrunk my
battlefield down to an island,

262
00:16:14,020 --> 00:16:17,700
Mako, but my stone soldier
still gets a field power bonus.

263
00:16:19,380 --> 00:16:22,960
Your massive monster can
barely fit on that little rock,

264
00:16:23,100 --> 00:16:26,041
let alone do battle with
my undersea attack force.

265
00:16:27,380 --> 00:16:30,520
And he is surrounded on
all sides by the ocean,

266
00:16:30,940 --> 00:16:34,640
making him easy prey
for Great White Terror.

267
00:16:38,500 --> 00:16:44,000
This savage shark will lead my other sea
creatures in an all-out ocean onslaught.

268
00:16:44,300 --> 00:16:46,817
Man, Yugi's guy is
outnumbered three to one.

269
00:16:46,900 --> 00:16:47,730
What?

270
00:16:47,813 --> 00:16:50,120
This stone soldier's
about to become fish food.

271
00:16:59,060 --> 00:17:00,437
This is it, Yu-Gi.

272
00:17:00,520 --> 00:17:03,220
It's over, but you played honorably.

273
00:17:03,620 --> 00:17:06,660
You have been a fair and
noble opponent too, Mako,

274
00:17:06,760 --> 00:17:09,936
but I also duel with the
fate of a loved one at stake.

275
00:17:11,280 --> 00:17:13,237
And I can't afford to lose.

276
00:17:13,320 --> 00:17:16,400
I switch my stone soldier to attack mode.

277
00:17:18,600 --> 00:17:19,860
Attack mode?

278
00:17:20,060 --> 00:17:20,980
But why?

279
00:17:21,460 --> 00:17:24,931
He cannot attack my sea monsters
while they are underwater.

280
00:17:25,220 --> 00:17:27,660
But his target isn't your sea monsters.

281
00:17:27,980 --> 00:17:31,900
I'm having him attack a card
I put on the field myself.

282
00:17:34,200 --> 00:17:35,380
The moon!

283
00:17:36,160 --> 00:17:36,990
No!

284
00:17:37,560 --> 00:17:40,660
Now, stone soldier, destroy the moon!

285
00:17:52,580 --> 00:17:58,317
what's happening the tide
it's going out but how

286
00:17:58,400 --> 00:18:02,717
as you yourself said before
mako it is the moon that

287
00:18:02,800 --> 00:18:07,157
controls the ocean's tides
its ebb and its flow so

288
00:18:07,240 --> 00:18:10,137
i ordered my stone soldier
to obliterate the moon,

289
00:18:10,220 --> 00:18:14,460
causing the ocean's tides to
reverse and recede. Power!

290
00:18:16,040 --> 00:18:18,657
My stone soldier has beached
all your sea monsters.

291
00:18:18,740 --> 00:18:20,460
You have no ocean left.

292
00:18:20,800 --> 00:18:22,920
No, my precious fish!

293
00:18:23,420 --> 00:18:25,840
And now I'll deliver the final blow.

294
00:18:27,500 --> 00:18:31,157
I combine my curse of dragon
card with the magic of the

295
00:18:31,240 --> 00:18:35,040
burning land card to wipe out
your remaining life points.

296
00:18:39,940 --> 00:18:41,260
Burning land attack!

297
00:18:43,440 --> 00:18:46,260
And that takes your life
points down to zero.

298
00:18:47,700 --> 00:18:48,530
No!

299
00:18:50,120 --> 00:18:52,260
Way to go, Yugi! Yes!

300
00:18:53,700 --> 00:18:57,935
Destroying your own moon card was a
brilliant and unexpected move, Yugi.

301
00:18:59,840 --> 00:19:01,280
What a grand duel.

302
00:19:01,540 --> 00:19:03,120
I salute you, my friend.

303
00:19:03,680 --> 00:19:06,620
This victory was not easily won, Mako.

304
00:19:06,780 --> 00:19:08,662
You're a great duelist yourself.

305
00:19:10,200 --> 00:19:12,220
I am down to one star, Chip.

306
00:19:12,520 --> 00:19:14,620
But I will start over again.

307
00:19:14,800 --> 00:19:16,480
And I bet you'll do fine.

308
00:19:16,780 --> 00:19:18,120
You'd win that wager.

309
00:19:19,980 --> 00:19:22,520
You know, I can't help but like that Mako.

310
00:19:22,620 --> 00:19:24,097
He's such a great guy and all.

311
00:19:24,180 --> 00:19:26,239
I hope he finds his father someday.

312
00:19:28,620 --> 00:19:31,060
My friend, dueling you is hungry work.

313
00:19:31,240 --> 00:19:33,780
Time for Mako to fish again. Beware!

314
00:19:37,860 --> 00:19:38,690
Bye, Mako.

315
00:19:38,800 --> 00:19:40,506
Wish he'd bring us some fish.

316
00:19:40,680 --> 00:19:42,327
We'd have to duel him again.

317
00:19:43,280 --> 00:19:44,380
Forget about it.

318
00:19:44,500 --> 00:19:46,277
But guys, I am getting seriously hungry.

319
00:19:46,360 --> 00:19:47,190
Not a problem.

320
00:19:47,273 --> 00:19:49,757
We've still got my great
outdoor survival guide.

321
00:19:49,840 --> 00:19:51,780
No way. Go ahead, Tristan.

322
00:19:51,960 --> 00:19:53,548
Eat all the pages you like.
